Z||000007||Cozmo||08-19-2001||10:45 AM||||Songman, I've been thinking the same thing...<BR>Here are some shifter assemblies from Summit's website<BR>BMM-80690 made by B&M<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BMM-80690.jpg"> <P>BMM-80676 made by B&M<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BMM-80676.jpg"> <P>HUU-H83-8520 made by Hurst<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/HUU-H383-8520_m.jpg"> <P>They all seem to be pretty universal mount with a 5 foot cable. This is the way I want to go, just got to see what mods (if any) are required...<BR>Anybody done it yet?<P><BR>BobC <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||08-19-2001||01:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cozmo:<BR><B><BR>BMM-80690 made by B&M<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BMM-80690.jpg">  <P>HUU-H83-8520 made by Hurst<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/HUU-H383-8520_m.jpg">  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, something like either of these was what I was wanting to do. Of course, I want to see what I can do for a complete new interior design anyway. I think the only problem with the shifter might be that Fiero shifters are cabled from the rear and most of these are from the front.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
Z||000009||Sleeper||08-19-2001||02:41 PM||||i don't think it has anything to do with shifters being cabled from the front or rear i think it has to do with the stock fiero transaxle(th-125) being to small. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/B&Mproratchet.jpg">  i've wanted this B&M Pro Ratchet for almost 2 years. my friend had it on his chevelle and it's a bad ass shifter, full ratchet 100% manual shifting without miss-shifting and screwing up your tranny.<P>well anyways i called b&m about two years ago and the tech there said our tranny in the fiero was too small and that the 4T60 was the smallest transaxle that would support a ratchet shifter. he also said that he knew of a few fieros off hand(at the time) that had their b&m shifters in fieros but they've used the 4T60 tranny. <P>------------------<BR>85 GT Auto<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels wrapped with Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering springs, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, West Coast Fiero Strut Tower Bar, West Coast Fiero Cold-Air Intake w/ HKS Super Flow filter, Beretta brake upgrade in front, KVS Performance Slotted Rotors in rear, Earl's Steel-Braided Brake Lines, custom burnt J.E.T. super chip and MSD Blaster Coil.<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/WCLogo6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cozmo||08-19-2001||04:28 PM||||What do you mean by "too small", Sleeper?<BR>The throw distance too short?<BR>?<BR>BobC||||reg||5
