Z||000015||Sleeper||08-20-2001||07:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cozmo:<BR><B>What do you mean by "too small", Sleeper?<BR>The throw distance too short?<BR>?<BR>BobC</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>dude, its like i said. the tech at b&m said that the th-125 is to small to support one of their shifters and he wouldn't advise me to do it. thats was about 2 years ago, you can always try and call if you like.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||3fifty||08-20-2001||09:07 PM||||Rob,<BR>The knob & shaft are one piece. The hollow shaft slides over the stock auto shaft once you sand all of the paint off of the factory<BR>shaft. I cut my factory shaft down one inch and then trimmed the plastic rod in the center to match. Rodney has boots also, but I used a Mr. Gasket boot from Auto Zone since I have the Pisa dash. Rodney gives you a stronger spring for the shifter. To shift just pust down and go to whatever gear. Push down and go back up to park and it pops up so the key will come out.||||reg||10
